Please find below items that we require RFIs for:

1. Fire hydrant booster and flow data

HY-003 shows a new 150 mm connection with DDCVA and meter and two dual-head hydrants, with no booster assembly. FC-101 shows the FRNSW hardstand. HY-002 requires the contractor to “provide flow test”. Please confirm that no hydrant booster assembly is required. Please also provide any available flow and pressure data for the existing Council main, or confirm that the flow test and any pump or booster resulting from it are to be priced provisionally.

2. Sewer connection and pump station

HY-003 states that the sewer discharge arrangement (pump station, Council connection, connection point, pipe sizes, invert levels and alignment) is to be designed, provided and approved by Council. Barnson’s design is limited to on-site drainage to the connection point nominated by Council. HY-200 notes that all invert levels are to be determined on site due to insufficient Council information. Please confirm:

(a) the works Council will carry out;

(b) the connection point and invert level the contractor is to drain to;

(c) any Council fees or works the contractor is to allow for.

3. Rail underbore

HY-003 shows an underbore beneath the railway tracks for the new water service, noted as “indicative only” and “to be confirmed with Council”, with the contractor to obtain rail authority approvals. Please confirm:

(a) which services cross the rail line;

(b) the required underbore length, method, sleeve and depth;

(c) the rail authority and its access, possession and approval requirements;

(d) whether this work is to be priced as a provisional sum.

4. Rainwater tank and re-use

CC03, CC05 and CC07 show a 26,000 L Kingspan RCT-25 tank with all roof water directed to it and a nominated “re-use volume”. The overflow goes “to water trough or other suitable location, TBD by client”. The hydraulic drawings (HY-100) show no rainwater re-use pump or reticulation to fixtures. Please confirm whether rainwater re-use (pump, controls and connection to WCs, urinals or hose taps) is required, and the overflow discharge location.

5. Kitchen equipment schedule

HY-100, HY-200 and EL-100 note that the final canteen and kitchen equipment schedule is to be provided by Council and was not available at CC documentation. Please provide the schedule, or confirm a PC sum or provisional allowance to be included for kitchen equipment and its services connections.

6. Security, access control and CCTV

Drawing EL-001 Rev 2 includes a legend for security and access devices (alarm panel, keypads, card readers, electric strikes and mag locks, PIRs, duress, intercom) and for CCTV (cameras, NVR, monitor). None of these devices are shown on EL-100, EL-200 or EL-201, and the Technical Specification (47181 Spec_A) has no security or CCTV section. EL-301 shows a security alarm interface to the external lighting control and space for a “future” CCTV NVR and monitor, with active equipment “by client”. Please confirm:

(a) whether an intruder alarm, access control and/or CCTV system is to be included in the contract works;

(b) if so, the device layout, coverage and performance requirements, and any Council standard system or brand to match existing DRLM security;

(c) if not, whether tenderers should allow for cabling and containment only, and to what extent.

